actually disruptors anymore.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.550
We've moved well beyond
the disruption phase.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.050
We're now officially
to the point

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.120
where these are just the
facts of our business.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.420
This is how we exist,
how we survive,

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.700
how we're actually
getting through, working

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.100
with the competition,
reaching our customers.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.380
Generational shifts are there.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.210
Pervasive connectivity.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.680
Everything is connected.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.300
Our devices are connected.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.260
We're doing competing
at the edge.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.320
We've got 5G that's
coming out and is

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.140
going to be widely adopted
within the next three years.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.600
Connectivity is at a rate
that we've never seen before.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.610
And the maturing technologies
are becoming mainstream.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.170
IA, machine learning,
blockchain--

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.790
these aren't new
concepts anymore.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.010
They're mainstream technologies.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.170
So we need to start
thinking about not

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.720
so much about digital
disruptors and more

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.250
about digital enablers.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.885
How are we enabling
our business?

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.540
OK, so here is the good news.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.230
This is, I think, where
the opportunity really is.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.792
So if you look at the numbers--

00:04:40.792 --> 00:04:41.750
so, a couple of things.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.540
I'm a consultant.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.150
I've been a consultant my entire
life until the last few years.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.313
And, as a consultant, I
