00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:01.350
So how is it that everybody
believes it's a priority?

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.870
The executives believe it's
going to be a differentiator.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.690
But nobody's seeing the results.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.720
It's a really, really
interesting thing.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.040
Oh, sorry, guys.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.010
It becomes more interesting
when you think about the why.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.780
My knee-jerk reaction
when I hear that

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.880
is, oh, well, they're
just not investing enough.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.490
They're not putting enough
money into these programs.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.020
They need to spend
more on digital.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.790
Then they'll see more results.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.130
Turns out, that's not
the answer, either.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.990
You look at what HBR,
Harvard Business Review,

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.260
has actually figured
out, if you look

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.750
at digital leaders, the
top 25% of adopters,

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:37.658
and digital laggards, the
bottom 25% of adopters,

00:06:37.658 --> 00:06:39.950
they are spending almost the
same exact amount of money

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.270
on IT.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.030
As a percentage of revenue,
it's almost exactly the same.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.420
It goes from 3.2% to 3.5%.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.410
That's the gap.

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.190
It's tiny.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.402
It's almost negligible.

00:06:50.402 --> 00:06:52.610
But if you look at the gap
in terms of their business

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.940
performance, it's amazing.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.250
80% improvement on
operating income.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.860
57% increase on profit line.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:05.120
So those are huge
results without a lot

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.560
of incremental spend.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.800
That's a huge opportunity.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.315
Sorry, guys, I'm
a little parched.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.880
I think I'm drinking water
out of a milk carton,

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.790
